  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist, and the rule is enabled and reporting status `ok`.\n\n**Data exploration**\n- The data view `kibana_sample_data_logs` has about 14,074 requests spanning 2026-10-04 to 2026-12-03, roughly 230 per day.\n- Key fields: `@timestamp` (time field), `response` / `response.keyword` (status code, stored as a string), `url`, `request`, `extension`, `geo.dest`, `clientip`, `bytes`, `agent`, and `host`.\n- Status codes are 200 (12,832), 404 (801), and 503 (441). 503 is the only 5xx code present.\n- The data runs past today (2026-10-12), so some of it is in the future relative to the current date.\n\n**Dashboard: `EFF-2c66e790 Web logs overview`**\n- ID: `eff-2c66e790-web-logs-overview-3bbefae96d3b`\n- Time range: 2026-10-01 to 2026-12-31, so it covers the whole dataset.\n- Panels:\n  1. Total requests (metric, count)\n  2. 5xx responses (metric, count filtered to `response.keyword` = 503)\n  3. Requests by response code (pie, terms on `response.keyword`)\n  4. Requests over time by response code (area, date histogram on `@timestamp`)\n- The area chart is not split by response code, despite its title. I should have either broken it down by `response.keyword` or renamed it. I can fix that with `update_panel` if you want.\n\n**Alert rule: `EFF-2c66e790 5xx spike`**\n- ID: `b842dc21-4bd6-44d3-9e45-28f5a2e28587`\n- Rule type: `.es-query` (Elasticsearch query), consumer `stackAlerts`, enabled.\n- Schedule: every 1 minute.\n- Condition: fires when the count of documents in the last 5 minutes is greater than 10.\n- Query: wildcard `response.keyword: 5*`, which matches any 5xx code.\n- Index: `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `@timestamp`.\n\nThe rule is set up correctly, but it will probably not fire on this data. The sample has only about 7 503s per day, so a 5-minute window will rarely reach 11. The rule is meant for live traffic.",
